      "id": "docs_platforms_adapters_platform_vs_delivery",
      "label": "Platform vs Delivery Adapter Distinction",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "rationale": "Platforms (platform-elysia, platform-hono, platform-h3) boot the module graph and own routing, whereas delivery adapters (serverless, hono, h3, nitro) translate envelopes and forward requests to an already-booted application without a second DI or route table.",
      "source_file": "docs/platforms/adapters.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
    {
      "id": "docs_platforms_adapters_two_adapter_shapes",
      "label": "KernelAdapter vs ApplicationAdapter",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "rationale": "KernelAdapter (Hono, H3) lowers the graph via createPlatformFactory and mounts routes on its router; ApplicationAdapter (Elysia) retains its native executor to preserve native validation, plugins, HandlerContext, and Eden types.",
      "source_file": "docs/platforms/adapters.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null
    },
